    "updated_at": "2025-01-16T06:54:34Z",
    "body": "While this doesn’t directly resolve what you’re asking for, did you consider embedding the SVG in a data URI? This seems to work for me in Firefox and Chrome (though I don’t know how to get Safari to properly render an SVG as a favicon even when referencing an external file)\n\n```html\n<link rel=\"icon\" href=\"data:image/svg+xml,<svg xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg' viewBox='0 0 100 100'><text y='.9em' font-size='90'>🌼</text></svg>\">\n```\n\nIt’s not as succinct as `content=\"🌼\"` but it also doesn’t require any exporting or build steps.",
